nction requireCapability(can: (role?: UserRole) => boolean): Promise<void> {\n       let role: UserRole | undefined\n       try { role = (await UsersService.readUserMe()).data.role }\n       catch { throw redirect({ to: \"/login\" }) }\n       if (!can(role)) { throw redirect({ to: \"/forbidden\" }) }\n     }\n     ```\n   - `frontend/src/routes/_layout/admin.tsx` — `beforeLoad: () => requireCapability(canListUsers)`; AddUser rendered only when `canManageUsers(currentUser?.role)`; columns filtered (`column.id !== \"actions\"`) for non-admin; heading \"Users\"\n   - `frontend/src/routes/_layout/metrics.tsx` — `beforeLoad: () => requireCapability(canViewMetrics)`; useSuspenseQuery on MetricsService.readMetricsSummary; Card grid of counts\n   - `frontend/src/routes/_layout/forbidden.tsx` — friendly Access-denied page with Back to Dashboard button\n   - `frontend/src/components/Sidebar/AppSidebar.tsx` — Metrics link (canViewMetrics), Users link (canListUsers) replacing is_superuser check\n   - `frontend/src/components/Admin/columns.tsx` — Role column shows `row.original.role` badge (variant default for admin)\n   - `frontend/src/main.tsx` — split handler (uncommitted):\n     ```ts\n     const handleUnauthorized = (error: Error) => {\n       if (error instanceof AxiosError && error.response?.status === 401) {\n         localStorage.removeItem(\"access_token\"); window.location.href = \"/login\"\n       }\n     }\n     // QueryCache onError: handleUnauthorized + 403 → window.location.href = \"/forbidden\"\n     // MutationCache onError: handleUnauthorized + 403 → toast.error(\"You don't have permission to perform this action\")\n     ```\n   - `frontend/src/routeTree.gen.ts` — regenerated via `../node_modules/.bin/vite build`\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - Bare `uv run pytest` failed (frontend dir RuntimeError) → tests need `FASTAPI_ENV=development` prefix (from scripts/test.sh)\n   - Ruff UP042 rejected `class UserRole(str, enum.Enum)` → changed to `enum.StrEnum`\n   - Repeated commit failures from \"Generate Frontend SDK\" prek hook regenerating client files as unstaged changes (\"Hook changes conflicted with the saved unstaged changes\") → must stage `frontend/src/client/*` regenerated files with each schema-changing commit; formatter rewraps also required re-stage + NEW commit (never --amend)\n   - ty check failed on metrics.py group_by dict (`dict[Unknown | Sequence[Unknown], int]`) → replaced with typed per-role count dict comprehension\n   - tsc failed: new routes not in stale routeTree.gen.ts → user REJECTED `bunx tsr generate`; fixed by running local `../node_modules/.bin/vite build` (plugin regenerates tree). Note: frontend has NO local node_modules — bun workspace hoists to repo root\n   - Two review agents claimed deps.py:39 `except A, B:` is a Python-2 SyntaxError blocker invalidating all test claims → REFUTED: verified `uv run python -m py_compile` OK on Python 3.14.6 (PEP 758), line verbatim from master, suite genuinely ran 84 passed\n   - `-k \"delete_user_super_user\"` matched wrong test (test_delete_user_super_user = superuser deletes another user); actual message test is `test_delete_user_current_super_user_error` → ran both by exact node ID, confirmed 2 red, then green after code change\n   - User's `/permissions` text message — explained it's a built-in CLI command I can't run; showed RBAC permission state table instead\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   Full TDD cycle executed for each milestone with red/green output shown. Data migration proven by forcing legacy state via psql then downgrade/upgrade. Review triage (receiving-code-review skill): ACCEPTED+IMPLEMENTED: main.tsx 401/403 split; requireCapability guard hardening (catch → /login); canViewMetrics independent; DELETE matrix rows (87 passed); self-delete logging + message change. REJECTED with reasoning: SyntaxError claim (false); require_roles tuple signature (mission mandates *roles); metrics query optimization; settings test-state leak; UserUpdate is_superuse