{"parentUuid":"ac9416a4-85f1-4586-b259-06795b386fb9","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"8b31c897-f54c-41b8-8cee-b76998fea3f7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011TKBLD6X6kviov593vedwL","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /home/dimakhaver/programming/EnderTuring/rbac-fastapi-task/README.md has been updated successfully."}]},"uuid":"b05957c4-489d-40d3-9692-7bb4517fa85a","timestamp":"2026-08-30T15:11:37.411Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"/home/dimakhaver/programming/EnderTuring/rbac-fastapi-task/README.md","oldString":"## How to Use It","newString":"## Role-Based Access Control (RBAC)\n\nThis fork adds three roles — `admin`, `manager`, `member` — enforced on the backend\nand mirrored in the frontend for UX. Design decisions are recorded in\n[docs/adr/001-role-model.md](./docs/adr/001-role-model.md) and\n[docs/adr/002-frontend-capability-propagation.md](./docs/adr/002-frontend-capability-propagation.md);\ndeliberate scope cuts in [NOTES.md](./NOTES.md).\n\n### Permission matrix\n\n| Action | admin | manager | member |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| List users (`GET /users/`) | ✓ | ✓ | ✗ |\n| Read any user (`GET /users/{id}`) | ✓ | ✓ | self only |\n| Create user (`POST /users/`) | ✓ | ✗ | ✗ |\n| Update/delete any user | ✓ | ✗ | ✗ |\n| Metrics (`GET /metrics/summary`) | ✓ | ✓ | ✗ |\n| Settings (`GET/PUT /settings/`) | ✓ | ✗ | ✗ |\n| Own profile view/update (`/users/me`) | ✓ | ✓ | ✓ |\n\nSemantics: **401** for missing/invalid credentials, **403** for authenticated but not\npermitted. Every denial is logged with user id and route. Public `POST /users/signup`\nstays open and always assigns `member`.\n\n### How it works\n\n- `role` is a single enum column on `User` and the sole source of truth for\n  authorization (`is_superuser` is kept only for template compatibility).\n- The role→permission mapping lives in one module:\n  [backend/app/api/permissions.py](./backend/app/api/permissions.py).\n- Routes are guarded declaratively with the `require_roles(*roles)` dependency\n  factory in [backend/app/api/deps.py](./backend/app/api/deps.py) — no inline role\n  checks in route bodies.\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n    A[Request] --> B{Valid JWT?}\n    B -- no --> C[401 Unauthorized]\n    B -- yes --> D[load User]\n    D --> E{\"user.role in\\nrequire_roles(...)?\"}\n    E -- no --> F[log denial\\n403 Forbidden]\n    E -- yes --> G[Route handler]\n```\n\n### Seeding roles\n\n- The first superuser (`FIRST_SUPERUSER` / `FIRST_SUPERUSER_PASSWORD` in `.env`) is\n  created with `role=admin` on prestart.\n- New signups get `role=member`.\n- To create a manager, log in as the admin and either use the API\n  (`PATCH /api/v1/users/{id}` with `{\"role\": \"manager\"}`) or run:\n  `docker compose exec db psql -U postgres -d app -c \"UPDATE \\\"user\\\" SET role='manager' WHERE email='...'\"`.\n\n### Running the RBAC tests\n\n```bash\ndocker compose up -d db mailpit\ncd backend && uv run bash scripts/test.sh\n```\n\nThe role×endpoint matrix lives in\n[backend/tests/api/routes/test_rbac.py](./backend/tests/api/routes/test_rbac.py).\n\n## How to Use It","originalFile":"# Full Stack FastAPI Template\n\n[![Test Docker Compose](../../actions/workflows/test-docker-compose.yml/badge.svg)](../../actions/workflows/test-docker-compose.yml)\n[![Test Backend](../../actions/workflows/test-backend.yml/badge.svg)](../../actions/workflows/test-backend.yml)\n\n## Technology Stack and Features\n\n- ⚡ [**FastAPI**](https://fastapi.tiangolo.com) for the Python backend API.\n  - 🧰 [SQLModel](https://sqlmodel.tiangolo.com) for the Python SQL database interactions (ORM).\n  - 🔍 [Pydantic](https://docs.pydantic.dev), used by FastAPI, for the data validation and settings management.\n  - 💾 [PostgreSQL](https://www.postgresql.org) as the SQL database.\n- 🚀 [React](https://react.dev) for the frontend.\n  - 🧩 Built into the backend application and served by FastAPI on the same domain as the API.\n  - 💃 Using TypeScript, hooks, [Vite](https://vitejs.dev), and other parts of a modern frontend stack.\n  - 🎨 [Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com) and [shadcn/ui](https://ui.shadcn.com) for the frontend components.\n  - 🤖 An automatically generated frontend client.\n  - 🧪 [Playwright](https://playwright.dev) for end-to-end testing.\n  - 🦇 Dark mode support.\n- ☁️ [FastAPI Cloud](https://fastapicloud.com) for deployment.\n- 🐋 [Docker Compose](https://www.docker.com) for local services and self-hosted deployment.\n  - 📞 [Traefik](https://traefik.io) as a reverse proxy with automatic HTTPS.\n- 🔒 Secure password hashing by default.\n- 🔑 JWT (JSON Web Token) authentication.\n- 📫 Email-based password recovery.\n- ✉️ [React Email](https://react.email) for email templates.\n- 📬 [Mailpit](https://mailpit.axllent.org) for local email testing during development.\n- ✅ Tests with [Pytest](https://pytest.org).\n- 🏭 CI (continuous integration) and CD (continuous deployment) based on GitHub Actions.\n\n### Dashboard Login\n\n![Dashboard login screenshot](img/login.png)\n\n### Dashboard - Admin\n\n![Admin dashboard screenshot](img/dashboard.png)\n\n### Dashboard - Items\n\n![Items dashboard screenshot](img/dashboard-items.png)\n\n### Dashboard - Dark Mode\n\n![Dark mode dashboard screenshot](img/dashboard-dark.png)\n\n### React Email Templates\n\n![Email templates screenshot](img/react-email.png)\n\n### Mailpit - Local Email Testing\n\n![Mailpit screenshot](img/mailpit.png)\n\n### Interactive API Documentation\n\n![API docs](img/docs.png)\n\n## How to Use It\n\nClick the **Use this template** button at the top of this page to create a new repository.\n\n## Backend Development\n\nBackend docs: [backend/README.md](./backend/README.md).\n\n## Frontend Development\n\nFrontend docs: [frontend/README.md](./frontend/README.md).\n\n## Deployment\n\nFastAPI Cloud deployment: [deployment.md](./deployment.md).\n\nSelf-hosted deployment with Docker Compose: [deployment-docker-compose.md](./deployment-docker-compose.md).\n\n## Development\n\nGeneral development docs: [development.md](./development.md).\n\nThis includes the local FastAPI and Vite workflow, Docker Compose services, `.env` configuration, and more.\n\n## Release Notes\n\nCheck the file [release-notes.md](./release-notes.md).\n\n## License\n\nThe Full Stack FastAPI Template is licensed under the terms of the MIT license.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":55,"oldLines":6,"newStart":55,"newLines":69,"lines":[" "," ![API docs](img/docs.png)"," ","+## Role-Based Access Control (RBAC)","+","+This fork adds three roles — `admin`, `manager`, `member` — enforced on the backend","+and mirrored in the frontend for UX. Design decisions are recorded in","+[docs/adr/001-role-model.md](./docs/adr/001-role-model.md) and","+[docs/adr/002-frontend-capability-propagation.md](./docs/adr/002-frontend-capability-propagation.md);","+deliberate scope cuts in [NOTES.md](./NOTES.md).","+","+### Permission matrix","+","+| Action | admin | manager | member |","+|---|---|---|---|","+| List users (`GET /users/`) | ✓ | ✓ | ✗ |","+| Read any user (`GET /users/{id}`) | ✓ | ✓ | self only |","+| Create user (`POST /users/`) | ✓ | ✗ | ✗ |","+| Update/delete any user | ✓ | ✗ | ✗ |","+| Metrics (`GET /metrics/summary`) | ✓ | ✓ | ✗ |","+| Settings (`GET/PUT /settings/`) | ✓ | ✗ | ✗ |","+| Own profile view/update (`/users/me`) | ✓ | ✓ | ✓ |","+","+Semantics: **401** for missing/invalid credentials, **403** for authenticated but not","+permitted. Every denial is logged with user id and route. Public `POST /users/signup`","+stays open and always assigns `member`.","+","+### How it works","+","+- `role` is a single enum column on `User` and the sole source of truth for","+  authorization (`is_superuser` is kept only for template compatibility).","+- The role→permission mapping lives in one module:","+  [backend/app/api/permissions.py](./backend/app/api/permissions.py).","+- Routes are guarded declaratively with the `require_roles(*roles)` dependency","+  factory in [backend/app/api/deps.py](./backend/app/api/deps.py) — no inline role","+  checks in route bodies.","+","+```mermaid","+flowchart LR","+    A[Request] --> B{Valid JWT?}","+    B -- no --> C[401 Unauthorized]","+    B -- yes --> D[load User]","+    D --> E{\"user.role in\\nrequire_roles(...)?\"}","+    E -- no --> F[log denial\\n403 Forbidden]","+    E -- yes --> G[Route handler]","+```","+","+### Seeding roles","+","+- The first superuser (`FIRST_SUPERUSER` / `FIRST_SUPERUSER_PASSWORD` in `.env`) is","+  created with `role=admin` on prestart.","+- New signups get `role=member`.","+- To create a manager, log in as the admin and either use the API","+  (`PATCH /api/v1/users/{id}` with `{\"role\": \"manager\"}`) or run:","+  `docker compose exec db psql -U postgres -d app -c \"UPDATE \\\"user\\\" SET role='manager' WHERE email='...'\"`.","+","+### Running the RBAC tests","+","+```bash","+docker compose up -d db mailpit","+cd backend && uv run bash scripts/test.sh","+```","+","+The role×endpoint matrix lives in","+[backend/tests/api/routes/test_rbac.py](./backend/tests/api/routes/test_rbac.py).","+"," ## How to Use It"," "," Click the **Use this template** button at the top of this page to create a new repository."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ac9416a4-85f1-4586-b259-06795b386fb9","userType":"external","cwd":"/home/dimakhaver/programming/EnderTuring/rbac-fastapi-task","sessionId":"4a1f3817-2385-4e23-95d7-028e997c9847","version":"2.1.74","gitBranch":"feature/rbac","slug":"jaunty-dancing-liskov"}
{"parentUuid":"b05957c4-489d-40d3-9692-7bb4517fa85a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CeZ9WtU8faRzovXs3oFfK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JFeMKPkzCd69NmXpjeCX92","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/dimakhaver/programming/EnderTuring/rbac-fastapi-task/docs/adr/001-role-model.md","content":"# ADR 001: Single role enum column as the source of truth\n\nStatus: accepted\n\n## Context\n\nThe template ships with a boolean `is_superuser` flag and a `get_current_active_superuser`\ndependency. The task requires three roles (admin, manager, member) with distinct\npermissions, and the design must make adding a role cheap and keep authorization\ngap-free.\n\nOptions considered:\n\n1. **Single `role` enum column on `User`** (chosen)\n2. Separate `Role`/`UserRole` tables (many-to-many)\n3. Permission strings per user (ACL-style)\n\n## Decision\n\nAdd `role: UserRole` (Postgres enum `admin | manager | member`, server default\n`member`) to the `user` table. `role` is the sole source of truth for authorization.\n\n- Central mapping in `app/api/permissions.py`: each protected capability is a tuple of\n  allowed roles (`LIST_USERS`, `MANAGE_USERS`, `READ_ANY_USER`, `VIEW_METRICS`,\n  `MANAGE_SETTINGS`).\n- One dependency factory `require_roles(*roles)` in `app/api/deps.py` guards routes\n  declaratively; `ensure_role()` handles the one conditional case (self-read of\n  `GET /users/{id}`). No role literals in route bodies.\n- Adding a role touches at most three files: `models.py` (enum member), a migration,\n  and `permissions.py` (grant capabilities).\n- Migration backfills `is_superuser=true → role=admin` and creates/drops the Postgres\n  enum explicitly for a clean round-trip.\n\n`is_superuser` is retained but no longer consulted on the RBAC surface — it stays only\nfor template compatibility (see NOTES.md for the remaining seams).\n\n## Consequences\n\n- Role checks are O(1) tuple membership; no joins, no extra queries.\n- Exactly one role per user — sufficient for this hierarchy; a role table would be\n  gold-plating at this scale and can be introduced later behind the same\n  `require_roles` seam.\n- 401 (missing/invalid credentials) and 403 (authenticated but forbidden) are strictly\n  separated, and every denial is logged with user id and route.\n- `UserUpdateMe`/`UserRegister` deliberately exclude `role`, so members cannot\n  escalate themselves; only admins (via `UserUpdate`) can change roles.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1573,"cache_read_input_tokens":52387,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1573},"output_tokens":21,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011CeZ9Wqq8bYqSMNT7MWxf3","type":"assistant","uuid":"fb2c5ac9-6011-4178-9a99-8f0895156764","timestamp":"2026-08-30T15:11:50.449Z","userType":"external","cwd":"/home/dimakhaver/programming/EnderTuring/rbac-fastapi-task","sessionId":"4a1f3817-2385-4e23-95d7-028e997c9847","version":"2.1.74","gitBranch":"feature/rbac","slug":"jaunty-dancing-liskov"}
